s  this jet puts out a good 105 horsepower  the street versions body design hardly  disguises its racecar origins  Kristoff's you a jet driver would have  to have an affinity for racing instead  of real car seats you lie in racing  bucket seats with your behind just above  the floor so it's nice and loud  the engine breeze down your neck when  there's no trace of noise insulation the  mantra seems oddly out of place like  some kind of spaceship against the  historical backdrop of Rivendell gardez  medieval belfry the story upon ollie  the streamlining of the fiberglass body  is interrupted only by the two air  scoops that who will be engine  the interior also reflects the racing  vibe a small steering wheel a short  gearshift and instruments everywhere  Krista thinks of Finnish sauna is  nothing compared to the mantra jet  he likes the flat windscreen but they  just make things hotter and the cooling  system is in front while the engine is  farther back and the hoses that connect  them run through the passenger  compartment the Finnish sauna feel is  rounded off by the hot engine mounted  behind the driver and insulated only by  this carpet the only thing to do is open  the roof but a sunroof was only  installed in 12 Jets this was because at  high speeds the wind could take out the  rear window just below the rear  windshield is the souped-up  four-cylinder engine developed by a me  day buddhini two dual carburetors  deliver high performance and Iran and  raspy sound the mantra jet was  originally conceived for the 24 Hours of  LeMans sports car races christophe  volume production was actually a kind of  byproduct clues are the custom-made  fiberglass body on a steel frame making  it very lightweight and the chassis with  formula three features also the  independent wishbone suspension and coil  springs  all this combined with a small steering  wheel allow the driver to take the  mantra in two curves with the greatest  of ease and precision  but the real novelty here is the  mid-engine before the jet only race cars  had ever placed the engine right by the  driver  it was mantra that brought this concept  out onto city streets  christos says only 1681 mantra jets were  ever built and it still made automotive  history as the first men engine car and  volume production and set a standard for  generations of super sports cars thanks  to the near-perfect weight distribution  52% in the back and 48% in front  it was absolutely unmatched in terms of  handling so it's without a doubt a  milestone in automotive history  it was also a trendsetter in the 1960s  ditomasso Lamborghini Lotus Ferrari  Porsche and almost every other  high-profile sports car maker brought  out a mid-engine car of their own
 

